# LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows checks out CRLF by default, which would make
# `prettier --check` and `cargo fmt --check` fail on Windows for files that
# are correct in the repository — a CI failure about line endings nobody
# introduced. Notes written by the app are LF too, so a vault copied between
# machines diffs cleanly.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and not to be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff2 binary
